 ```
 
+Footnotes are numbered and listed in the order in which they are first referenced
+in the document, regardless of the order in which they are defined. Footnotes
+which are only referenced from within other footnotes follow the footnotes which
+reference them, and footnotes which are never referenced are listed last in the
+order in which they are defined. To number and list footnotes in the order in
+which they are defined instead, set the `USE_DEFINITION_ORDER` option to `True`.
+
